  "behavior": [
    "PreparedDecodeSource lowers actual added-first normalized lookup and special filtering into exact immutable record/byte storage, supporting plain join and ByteLevel whole-token fallback.",
    "The source-bound layout checks arithmetic and all exact history/raw/candidate/prefix destinations before mutation; total successful calls remain finite across history compaction.",
    "Streaming output and retained frontier match the pinned HF helper; borrowed chunks exclude concurrent buffer mutation. InvalidPrefix preserves its appended frontier; limit rejection mutates none.",
    "Execution survives dropping the original HF snapshots and wrapper; cold compilation and original source ownership remain separate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No original registration, provider, one-use admission bank, accounting hold or managed public route is added.",
    "Cold HF compilation peaks, enclosing tokenizer ownership, parser/events/escaped errors and copied source/state destinations are not covered by final buffer diagnostics.",
    "Other decoder forms keep legacy behavior and receive a typed unsupported lowering from this incomplete mechanism; no architectural inapplicability is claimed.",
    "The seeded InvalidPrefix test checks a diagnostic frontier, not a naturally occurring error in fresh supported programs."
  ]
